# web/ — Rails 8 Conventions

Stack is locked in `docs/web-stack.md`. Ruby 3.3, Rails 8. Granular coding standards live in `docs/guidelines/web/`.

## Architecture
- Business logic in **service objects** (`app/services/`, e.g. `Communication::SendMessage`). HTML and API controllers both delegate to services — no duplicated rules.
- Authorization via **Pundit** policies (`app/policies/`); roles: backoffice, school, teacher, guardian.
- Web UI: Hotwire (Turbo + Stimulus) + Tailwind + ViewComponent. Server-rendered HTML by default; add JS only when Turbo/Stimulus can't solve it.
- API: REST JSON, versioned under `/api/v1`, JWT auth for mobile.

## Infra defaults (MVP)
- PostgreSQL 16+, Solid Queue (jobs), Solid Cache. No Redis/Sidekiq in MVP.
- Active Storage → S3. Push via FCM, enqueued on Solid Queue, gated by a state machine.

## Testing
RSpec (unit/model/service + request specs), Capybara + Cuprite (system), FactoryBot.

## Pending decisions — do not choose unilaterally
Serialization (`jsonapi-serializer` vs `blueprinter`), web auth (Rails 8 gen vs Devise), and JSON key casing are open in `docs/open-questions.md`. Flag them instead of assuming.

## Out of scope
Separate JS SPA (React/Vue on web), GraphQL, microservices, Sidekiq/Redis for jobs.
